```rust
let local_terminal = match &body {
    RequestBody::AttachTerminal { terminal, .. }
    | RequestBody::DetachTerminal { terminal } => Some(*terminal),
    _ => None,
};
let attaching = matches!(body, RequestBody::AttachTerminal { .. });
...
let response = endpoint.request(remote).await;
if let Some(terminal) = local_terminal
    && attaching != response.is_ok()
{
    sessions::on_detach(&self.terminal_frames, host, terminal);
}
```
For `DetachTerminal`, `attaching == false`; when the remote errors, `response.is_ok() == false`, the condition is false and `on_detach` is skipped. The remote side rejects a detach for a terminal it has already forgotten: `Sessions::detach` starts with `self.host_or_not_found(terminal)?` (crates/fleet-daemon/src/services/sessions/host_bridge.rs:34-35), which returns `DaemonError::NotFound`.

